{"meta": {"limit": 100, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 5}, "objects": [{"abstract": "   This draft defines a new TLS Certificate Compression scheme which\n   uses a shared dictionary of root and intermediate WebPKI\n   certificates.  The scheme smooths the transition to post-quantum\n   certificates by eliminating the root and intermediate certificates\n   from the TLS certificate chain without impacting trust negotiation.\n   It also delivers better compression than alternative proposals whilst\n   ensuring fair treatment for both CAs and website operators.  It may\n   also be useful in other applications which store certificate chains,\n   e.g.  Certificate Transparency logs.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-cert-abridge/", "expires": "2024-03-09T14:39:11Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 345263, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-cert-abridge", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 19, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/345263/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2023-11-04T12:02:09Z", "title": "Abridged Compression for WebPKI Certificates", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This draft defines a new TLS Certificate Compression scheme which\n   uses a shared dictionary of root and intermediate WebPKI\n   certificates.  The scheme smooths the transition to post-quantum\n   certificates by eliminating the root and intermediate certificates\n   from the TLS certificate chain without impacting trust negotiation.\n   It also delivers better compression than alternative proposals whilst\n   ensuring fair treatment for both CAs and website operators.  It may\n   also be useful in other applications which store certificate chains,\n   e.g.  Certificate Transparency logs.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-cert-abridge/", "expires": "2024-03-09T14:39:11Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 341191, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-cert-abridge", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 19, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/341191/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2023-09-06T14:39:11Z", "title": "Abridged Compression for WebPKI Certificates", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This draft defines a new TLS Certificate Compression scheme which\n   uses a shared dictionary of root and intermediate WebPKI\n   certificates.  The scheme smooths the transition to post-quantum\n   certificates by eliminating the root and intermediate certificates\n   from the TLS certificate chain without impacting trust negotiation.\n   It also delivers better compression than alternative proposals whilst\n   ensuring fair treatment for both CAs and website operators.  It may\n   also be useful in other applications which store certificate chains,\n   e.g.  Certificate Transparency logs.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-cert-abridge/", "expires": "2024-09-17T14:09:25Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 356210, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-cert-abridge", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 21, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/356210/", "rev": "01", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [],